 				<p epub:type="z3998:salutation">“Dear Jo,</p>
 				<p>“What ho!</p>
 				<p>“Some English girls and boys are coming to see me tomorrow and I want to have a jolly time. If it’s fine, I’m going to pitch my tent in Longmeadow, and row up the whole crew to lunch and croquet⁠—have a fire, make messes, gypsy fashion, and all sorts of larks. They are nice people, and like such things. Brooke will go, to keep us boys steady, and Kate Vaughn will play propriety for the girls. I want you all to come; can’t let Beth off, at any price, and nobody shall worry her. Don’t bother about rations⁠—I’ll see to that, and everything else⁠—only do come, there’s a good fellow!</p>
